{"version": "6.9", "hitCount": 2, "request": {"queryString": "\"PSCA\" AND lacrimal AND \"Homo sapiens\"[Organism]", "resultType": "core", "cursorMark": "*", "pageSize": 5, "sort": "", "synonym": false}, "resultList": {"result": [{"id": "23674615", "source": "MED", "pmid": "23674615", "pmcid": "PMC3734586", "fullTextIdList": {"fullTextId": ["PMC3734586"]}, "doi": "10.1074/mcp.m112.024075", "title": "Mapping the extracellular and membrane proteome associated with the vasculature and the stroma in the embryo.", "authorString": "Soulet F, Kilarski WW, Roux-Dalvai F, Herbert JM, Sacewicz I, Mouton-Barbosa E, Bicknell R, Lalor P, Monsarrat B, Bikfalvi A.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Soulet F", "lastName": "Soulet", "firstName": "Fabienne", "initials": "F", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "INSERM, U1029, 33405 Talence, France."}]}}, {"fullName": "Kilarski WW", "lastName": "Kilarski", "firstName": "Witold W", "initials": "WW", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0734-4749"}}, {"fullName": "Roux-Dalvai F", "lastName": "Roux-Dalvai", "firstName": "Florence", "initials": "F", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-9961-8964"}}, {"fullName": "Herbert JM", "lastName": "Herbert", "firstName": "John M J", "initials": "JM"}, {"fullName": "Sacewicz I", "lastName": "Sacewicz", "firstName": "Izabela", "initials": "I", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3071-4093"}}, {"fullName": "Mouton-Barbosa E", "lastName": "Mouton-Barbosa", "firstName": "Emmanuelle", "initials": "E", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7793-4560"}}, {"fullName": "Bicknell R", "lastName": "Bicknell", "firstName": "Roy", "initials": "R", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0941-8919"}}, {"fullName": "Lalor P", "lastName": "Lalor", "firstName": "Patricia", "initials": "P", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-8733-5273"}}, {"fullName": "Monsarrat B", "lastName": "Monsarrat", "firstName": "Bernard", "initials": "B"}, {"fullName": "Bikfalvi A", "lastName": "Bikfalvi", "firstName": "Andreas", "initials": "A"}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-8733-5273"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0941-8919"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3071-4093"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7793-4560"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-9961-8964"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0734-4749"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0005-7459-8580"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "8", "volume": "12", "journalIssueId": 2062181, "dateOfPublication": "2013 Aug", "monthOfPublication": 8, "yearOfPublication": 2013, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Mol Cell Proteomics", "title": "Molecular & cellular proteomics : MCP", "essn": "1535-9484", "issn": "1535-9476", "isoabbreviation": "Mol Cell Proteomics", "nlmid": "101125647"}, "printPublicationDate": "2013-08-01"}, "pubYear": "2013", "pageInfo": "2293-2312", "abstractText": "In order to map the extracellular or membrane proteome associated with the vasculature and the stroma in an embryonic organism in vivo, we developed a biotinylation technique for chicken embryo and combined it with mass spectrometry and bioinformatic analysis. We also applied this procedure to implanted tumors growing on the chorioallantoic membrane or after the induction of granulation tissue. Membrane and extracellular matrix proteins were the most abundant components identified. Relative quantitative analysis revealed differential protein expression patterns in several tissues. Through a bioinformatic approach, we determined endothelial cell protein expression signatures, which allowed us to identify several proteins not yet reported to be associated with endothelial cells or the vasculature. This is the first study reported so far that applies in vivo biotinylation, in combination with robust label-free quantitative proteomics approaches and bioinformatic analysis, to an embryonic organism. It also provides the first description of the vascular and matrix proteome of the embryo that might constitute the starting point for further developments.", "affiliation": "INSERM, U1029, 33405 Talence, France.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Journal Article"]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Intestine, Small", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "EM", "qualifierName": "embryology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Liver", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "EM", "qualifierName": "embryology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Kidney", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "EM", "qualifierName": "embryology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Chorioallantoic Membrane", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "IN", "qualifierName": "injuries"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Cell Line, Tumor"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Endothelial Cells", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Chick Embryo", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Animals"